@inject IJSRuntime JS

@*
    Renders nothing. Scrolls the page to the top once, when the results view appears.

    Every calculator is one page with two views: the input form, then the results in
    its place. Pressing Calculate at the bottom of a long form swapped the view and
    left the scroll position untouched, so on gear-pair or torsion-spring the reader
    was left looking at the middle of a results table with no sign that the top of the
    page had changed. Nothing in the app called scrollTo at all before this.

    Why a component inside the results block rather than a line in each Calculate():
    the trigger wanted is "the results view is now on screen", and that is exactly when
    this component is created. Blazor disposes the subtree of the @if branch that went
    away and builds the new one, so firstRender is true each time the page flips from
    the form to the results - including the flip a restored share link causes, and the
    one after Back to Input and Calculate again. It also keeps the scroll out of the
    calculation path, where a JS interop failure has no business being.

    Usage: put <ScrollToResults /> at the top of the results branch.
*@

@code {
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (!firstRender) return;

        try
        {
            await JS.InvokeVoidAsync("mekanikaScrollToTop");
        }
        catch
        {
            // Scrolling is a courtesy. An old cached index.html without js/shell.js,
            // or JS blocked outright, must not throw out of a render.
        }
    }
}
